To ensure basic functionality, a couple of things on the new system need to be
set up. These include:
    - swap and/or zram
    - an fstab file for mounting volumes at boot
    - the system clock and time settings
    - locale(s)
    - network interfaces
    - a root password

You will be prompted for customization options throughout the process. This is a
rather involved step so it is designed in a more modular way: You will be
offered to skip each part before it is run. Be careful however, as skipping a
section entirely will result in an incomplete and possibly non-functional
system.
